                    "id": 17592186096617,
                    "title": "Differentiating a Product Containing a Trigonometric Function"
                  },
                  "markdown": "Differentiate $x\\cos x.$",
                  "mathAcademyId": "e-3634",
                  "requiresCalculator": null,
                  "solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=\\cos x .$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\t (x\\cos x)' &=   u'(x) \\cdot v(x) + u(x) \\cdot v'(x)\\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t&= (x)'\\cdot \\cos x + x\\cdot (\\cos x)'\\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t   & = 1 \\cdot \\cos x + x (-\\sin x)\\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t  & =  \\cos x - x \\sin x\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
                  "status": "completed",
                  "stepId": "17592186097426",
                  "title": "Differentiating a Product Containing a Trigonometric Function"
                },
                "total": 5
