                  "markdown": "Differentiate $(4 - x^{2})(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)}).$",
                  "mathAcademyId": null,
                  "requiresCalculator": null,
                  "solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=4 - x^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\tan{\\left(x \\right)}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}((4 - x^{2})(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)}))^{'} & =u'(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot v'(x) \\\\ & =(4 - x^{2})'\\cdot (\\tan{\\left(x \\right)})+(4 - x^{2})\\cdot (\\tan{\\left(x \\right)})' \\\\ & =(- 2 x)(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)})+(4 - x^{2})(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1) \\\\ & =- x^{2} \\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} - x^{2} - 2 x \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 4 \\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
