                    "title": "Differentiating a Product Containing a Trigonometric Function"
                  },
                  "markdown": "Differentiate $(4 x^{4} + x)(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 2).$",
                  "mathAcademyId": null,
                  "requiresCalculator": null,
                  "solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=4 x^{4} + x$ and $v(x)=\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 2.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}((4 x^{4} + x)(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 2))^{'} & =u'(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot v'(x) \\\\ & =(4 x^{4} + x)'\\cdot (\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 2)+(4 x^{4} + x)\\cdot (\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 2)' \\\\ & =(16 x^{3} + 1)(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 2)+(4 x^{4} + x)(\\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1) \\\\ & =4 x^{4} \\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 4 x^{4} + 16 x^{3} \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 32 x^{3} + x \\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + x + \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} + 2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
                  "status": "correct",
                  "stepId": "17592186097426",
                  "title": "Differentiating a Product Containing a Trigonometric Function"
                },
                "total": 5
              },
