                  },
                  "markdown": "Given that $f(x)=x^2\\ln x,$ find $f'(x).$",
                  "mathAcademyId": "e-3635",
                  "requiresCalculator": null,
                  "solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x) = x^2$ and $v(x)=\\ln x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({x}^{2})}^{′}ln⁡x+{x}^{2}{(ln⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot ln⁡x+{x}^{2}(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =2xln⁡x+x \\\\  & =x(2ln⁡x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
                  "status": "completed",
